{
  "bio": [
    "David Kabiller is a cofounder and head of business development at AQR, a quantitative investment firm with $187 billion in assets under management.",
    "AQR stands for Applied Quantitative Research. It invests based on quantitative and proprietary signals, offering products including hedge funds, mutual funds and separately managed accounts.",
    "The firm is headquartered in Greenwich, Connecticut, with other locations in Bangaluru, Dubai, Hong Kong, London, Munich and Sydney.",
    "Before AQR, he was a vice president at Goldman Sachs, working with chief investment officers of large pension and endowment funds in North America."
  ],
  "about": [
    "Kabiller founded the Kabiller Prize and the Kabiller Young Investigator Award for researchers in nanoscience and nanomedicine at Northwestern University.",
    "At Northwestern, his alma mater, Kabiller has founded a series of prizes and awards in the field of nanoscience and nanomedicine."
  ]
}